  LocalProfileNotes: "LOCAL PLAYTEST PROFILE v2 \u2014 local controls and undefined
    content remain provisional.\nManhattan ranges and effect radius N. Attacks retain
    their reserved target and range eligibility. Same-phase attacks remain valid;
    HP updates per attack and deaths settle at phase end.\nPhases 0\u20134: revive
    at 0; movement advances concurrently by tile within each movement phase. First
    item contact wins; contacts tied in one step award each team once and remove
    the item immediately.\nBurn hits on creation and at its original skill phase
    on later turns; duration includes the creation turn and has no movement-entry
    damage. Stealth and root share status-effect definitions; operational beacons
    detect stealth.\nKill AP is awarded at turn wrap, capped at 25, with a visible
    actual-increase cue. Death clears all cooldowns. Revive next turn at full HP
    in own base vision, cost 15 decreasing to 10, clearing status effects and preventing
    another action that turn.\nEquipment decks contain 1\u20135 distinct reusable
    crafting choices; only three item types are currently defined. Crafting replaces
    equipment only after confirmation and resets its cooldown. Overlapping swaps
    and installation claims fail without cost. Portal progress includes its creation
    turn and completes at phase 4 end; linked ends die together.\nReady may be unlocked
    before planning ends; both ready or the deadline starts one resolution. Enemy
    identity and confirmed death are public; hidden revival requires observation,
    and hidden paths or attack sources are not replayed.\nUndefined upgrades, consumables,
    progression, online play and final input choices await their documented decisions."
